    <string name="shizuku_guide_title_not_installed">Shizuku not installed</string>
    <string name="shizuku_guide_body_not_installed">This engine needs the official Shizuku APK.\n\nPrefer one APK? Switch Killer Engine to «Built-in (ADB)» in Settings — no Shizuku required.\n\nOr download Shizuku, start it via Wireless debugging, then authorize.</string>
    <string name="shizuku_guide_title_not_running">Start privilege service</string>
    <string name="shizuku_guide_body_not_running">Built-in mode: no official Shizuku APK needed.\n\n1. Enable Developer options → Wireless debugging.\n2. (First time) Pair device with pairing code — enter the 6-digit code below and tap Pair.\n3. Tap Start service (app connects to adbd and launches its private privilege process).\n4. After every reboot, turn Wireless debugging on and Start again.\n\nManual fallback: run the starter command from a PC already on adb (shown after dump).</string>
    <string name="shizuku_guide_title_not_authorized">Authorize KillMyApps</string>
    <string name="shizuku_guide_body_not_authorized">Shizuku is running. Tap Authorize to grant this app permission to force-stop packages.</string>
